WEBVTT

00:20.410 --> 00:21.660
Why are you laughing?

00:22.250 --> 00:23.620
Now behave and come with—

00:30.050 --> 00:32.420
Am I not allowed to laugh?!

00:41.310 --> 00:43.770
Someone...

00:43.770 --> 00:46.100
In that case, do me a favor...

00:46.940 --> 00:48.230
And cry.

00:50.570 --> 00:53.610
Someone!

01:02.120 --> 01:07.710
The Dark Metal

01:02.120 --> 01:02.160
The Dark Metal

01:07.710 --> 01:12.130
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

01:12.130 --> 01:16.300
Where did the person I want to meet go?

01:16.300 --> 01:20.760
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

01:20.760 --> 01:24.520
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

01:24.560 --> 01:29.150
When the flower's petals

01:29.150 --> 01:33.280
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

01:33.280 --> 01:37.740
They are scattered in every direction

01:37.740 --> 01:43.080
Even if you long for it

01:44.080 --> 01:48.790
Do it without disappearing

01:48.790 --> 01:52.590
I can even give everything else away if I have to

01:52.590 --> 01:57.430
You were there, and I was there with you

01:57.430 --> 02:01.760
Let me take in these memories

02:01.760 --> 02:08.690
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

02:25.500 --> 02:30.500
Episode 2
Embraced by the Reaper

02:31.750 --> 02:36.300
The large Admonition that appeared late last night

02:36.300 --> 02:38.800
near Kawadahara's Mt. Benten
was defeated by the students

02:38.800 --> 02:42.300
assigned to Kukunochi's new
special investigation team.

02:42.300 --> 02:46.390
I was so scared!

02:46.390 --> 02:50.270
And when I think about having to fight things like that again...

02:51.270 --> 02:53.020
I'll protect you!

02:53.270 --> 02:54.150
You idiot!

02:54.150 --> 02:57.940
There's no way you can protect Emiru-san, who's in the pilot course.

02:58.650 --> 03:00.030
Hey, Akashi-kun!

03:00.530 --> 03:02.950
Did you really fight an Admonition?

03:02.950 --> 03:04.240
Weren't you scared?

03:04.240 --> 03:07.330
You'll have to make it into the pilot course first.

03:07.330 --> 03:08.330
Thanks, guys.

03:08.330 --> 03:10.210
I'm happy you all feel that way!

03:12.210 --> 03:14.880
But Akashi will be the one protecting me.

03:14.880 --> 03:16.500
Really?

03:22.640 --> 03:23.850
Let go.

03:23.850 --> 03:26.760
Oh, there's no need to be bashful.

03:26.760 --> 03:28.100
You smell bad.

03:28.100 --> 03:29.350
Wha—

03:30.020 --> 03:31.350
Hold on!

03:31.350 --> 03:33.310
Are you still holding a grudge
because I called you an impot—?

03:41.610 --> 03:46.370
You just don't get hungry when you're having flashbacks about Corpses, right?

03:46.620 --> 03:48.040
The nondisclosure agreement...

03:48.040 --> 03:49.870
No one will hear us.

03:52.750 --> 03:55.290
That was the first time I've ever seen a Corpse.

03:55.750 --> 03:58.500
I had heard rumors about them from all my coworkers,

03:59.130 --> 04:01.840
but I always thought they'd look more like Admonitions.

04:02.840 --> 04:03.930
Yeah.

04:03.930 --> 04:08.220
That wasn't about how big it was or what shape it had.

04:09.140 --> 04:11.600
It wasn't like it was attacking us,

04:12.140 --> 04:17.690
but it still felt like my soul was
being crushed by its cold grip.

04:17.690 --> 04:19.610
I know, right?

04:19.610 --> 04:22.490
And there's something else on my mind.

04:22.490 --> 04:23.570
When it happened...

04:23.860 --> 04:25.410
Over here.

04:27.410 --> 04:30.290
We all heard the same voice.

04:30.870 --> 04:33.750
The instructor didn't hear any of it, though.

04:33.750 --> 04:35.880
So why were we the only ones?

04:35.880 --> 04:36.880
Over here.

04:38.090 --> 04:39.250
I hear it after all!

04:39.840 --> 04:40.840
Raika.

04:41.840 --> 04:45.550
If you can't finish it off, give Minashi some of your udon.

04:53.480 --> 04:54.850
Udon!

04:54.850 --> 04:57.980
You already ate your share, House!

04:59.480 --> 05:00.190
You're cheap!

05:03.190 --> 05:05.450
Is he really as old as we are?

05:06.660 --> 05:08.910
Aren't you mistaking him for a grade schooler?

05:09.870 --> 05:11.660
What foolishness!

05:11.660 --> 05:14.370
That's why I say women shouldn't be pilots!

05:14.370 --> 05:16.000
S-Sorry.

05:17.170 --> 05:21.670
Maybe these ridiculously huge knockers are getting in your way?

05:21.670 --> 05:23.880
Instructor! That's sexual harassment!

05:23.880 --> 05:26.260
I'll be going to your dorm tonight!

05:26.260 --> 05:30.390
I'll pound what it means to be a pilot into you!

05:28.800 --> 05:30.390
Are you okay?

05:30.390 --> 05:32.060
I'm so happy!

05:32.350 --> 05:36.270
I've been wanting to learn all <i>sorts</i> of things from you!

05:37.810 --> 05:39.230
S-Sure...

05:39.610 --> 05:41.360
I'll be waiting for you!

05:40.270 --> 05:41.940
First victim confirmed.

05:42.480 --> 05:45.440
You're a female, but you have some potential.

05:44.320 --> 05:46.030
Oh, it's nothing...

05:46.030 --> 05:48.660
Really? I'm so glad!

06:06.220 --> 06:08.470
"I'll be waiting for you," she says...

06:45.460 --> 06:47.380
Maybe that old man isn't showing?

06:48.050 --> 06:49.970
This bothers me a little.

06:49.970 --> 06:51.220
Really?

06:51.590 --> 06:54.970
He did hear the Corpse's song, after all.

06:56.890 --> 06:57.730
I'll go take a look.

06:59.230 --> 07:01.770
You worried about a guy like that?

07:01.770 --> 07:04.150
I'm tired of training indoors.

07:04.150 --> 07:05.940
In fact, if we say we're looking for him,

07:06.280 --> 07:08.990
it'd give us a reason to go outside.

07:09.860 --> 07:11.110
It's a good opportunity.

07:11.110 --> 07:13.660
I-I'll come with you, Akashi!

07:13.660 --> 07:14.490
I'll go as well!

07:16.580 --> 07:18.330
A nighttime stroll!

07:20.920 --> 07:23.290
He's pretty darn serious.

07:23.290 --> 07:24.670
Who? Akashi?

07:24.670 --> 07:28.260
I thought he wasn't as good as he pretended to be.

07:28.260 --> 07:32.220
Well, I've known him ever since we were just kids...

07:32.220 --> 07:37.390
I can't remember when it was, but one day he started beating himself up.

07:37.680 --> 07:42.560
You could say he was stoic,
but it felt like he was being haunted.

07:42.560 --> 07:43.730
Chased?

07:43.730 --> 07:46.650
Well, it's possible that he just likes pain.

07:48.730 --> 07:53.240
That sexually harassing instructor, and that slutty bitch too...

07:56.740 --> 08:00.200
But it may not be that interesting if it's completely one-sided.

08:01.830 --> 08:04.670
I'm gonna need strong reinforcements on the IX side...

08:04.670 --> 08:05.960
Oh, I know!

08:24.980 --> 08:26.480
The Corpse's song...

08:27.690 --> 08:28.860
Oh, sorry.

08:28.860 --> 08:32.190
Man, I love the smell of the night!

08:32.740 --> 08:35.530
Hey, are you still upset?

08:35.530 --> 08:38.240
We're in this together, so let's be friends.

08:39.620 --> 08:42.080
Don't tell me I smell again, okay?

08:42.080 --> 08:44.620
I took a bath and everything for this.

08:45.080 --> 08:47.130
That won't make it go away.

08:48.250 --> 08:52.880
The smell of your obscenity has
seeped in much deeper than that.

08:52.880 --> 08:53.720
Obscen—?

08:54.220 --> 08:56.470
I'm going back!

08:57.850 --> 09:01.430
Come on, Akashi, you shouldn't get into fights!

09:02.480 --> 09:04.770
Suspicions of Caron and Garon...

09:05.600 --> 09:12.820
One, meddling in affairs of crying children...

09:06.940 --> 09:08.400
This song...

09:13.780 --> 09:20.580
Two, burn the bones of crying children...

09:20.580 --> 09:27.540
Three, atop the carcass is a crying child...

09:28.460 --> 09:32.670
Quiet, just be quiet, suspicions of the corpses.

09:32.670 --> 09:37.760
Scattered into ashes, here, Garon...

09:45.680 --> 09:48.350
The instructor's been killed...

09:57.360 --> 09:59.910
It tastes like he felt terror as he died.

10:10.630 --> 10:11.880
What is this?

10:16.010 --> 10:20.930
He always thought of his students and respectably fulfilled all of his duties.

10:21.550 --> 10:26.060
Let us have a moment of silence to
wish our dear teacher, Mr Niegawa, off.

10:26.060 --> 10:27.140
May he rest in peace.

10:30.600 --> 10:32.060
Just like the rumor goes.

10:33.400 --> 10:37.240
Those unfortunate enough to hear the Corpse's song will die within nine days.

10:38.360 --> 10:39.610
Mahmu!

10:40.450 --> 10:42.160
Iwato, don't scare her off!

10:42.660 --> 10:43.910
Fine.

10:53.250 --> 10:55.420
I smell terror...

11:07.600 --> 11:08.770
Amazing!

11:09.480 --> 11:10.980
You were right.

11:11.560 --> 11:12.520
Emiru-san...

11:15.900 --> 11:17.030
Why?

11:17.360 --> 11:20.200
This was quite the read.

11:20.200 --> 11:24.870
The first victim being the
instructor was a pretty keen point.

11:24.870 --> 11:28.450
T-That's not it! It's just fiction. Or rather...

11:28.450 --> 11:30.790
Yet you use real names?

11:30.790 --> 11:32.000
T-That's...

11:32.830 --> 11:36.380
So I'm going to be the next victim?

11:36.380 --> 11:38.170
T-That's not—

11:38.170 --> 11:40.720
I have one thing I want to ask.

11:40.720 --> 11:42.930
What's this so-called Reaper you write about here?

11:44.680 --> 11:51.480
"Hazaki Emiru falls prey to the Corpse, and a rumor starts to circulate within the academy.

11:51.480 --> 11:55.980
It says that the Reaper can defeat the Corpse."

11:57.780 --> 11:59.860
There was a rumor for a while.

12:00.440 --> 12:04.030
There's a hospital that's no longer in use now.

12:04.030 --> 12:04.950
And there...

12:05.660 --> 12:06.660
A hospital?

12:07.160 --> 12:10.620
We have a casualty in our personnel?

12:10.910 --> 12:12.790
That's actually good news.

12:12.790 --> 12:16.380
Now we have a reason to demand
more federal funding for development.

12:16.380 --> 12:20.420
However, if they decide to audit us using this as an excuse...

12:22.220 --> 12:23.720
I'm aware of that.

12:26.600 --> 12:31.770
Before that happens, I need to
implement the Mavess system.

12:32.520 --> 12:36.650
Fortunately, I have a good idea who the pilot will be.

12:36.650 --> 12:37.900
Leave it to us.

12:39.020 --> 12:40.480
Wait a moment.

12:40.480 --> 12:42.780
Are you really going to make <i>him</i> pilot the Argent?

12:43.530 --> 12:49.160
Kasane, personal devotion is
something unnecessary for a scholar.

12:49.160 --> 12:50.160
But!

12:50.160 --> 12:51.620
Chief Natsuiri.

12:51.620 --> 12:52.710
Look at this.

12:56.040 --> 12:57.000
This is...

12:58.130 --> 13:02.340
The Argent—no, the Reaper, is calling...

13:02.340 --> 13:04.970
Calling for the children of destiny...

13:08.010 --> 13:11.850
This hospital was apparently where
most of the people where brought to

13:11.850 --> 13:14.560
when the Lightless Realm was first created.

13:14.560 --> 13:17.480
But not a single person survived.

13:18.060 --> 13:19.190
Probably.

13:19.190 --> 13:21.530
This place feels like a dump.

13:22.030 --> 13:24.610
They say the souls of those who passed away here

13:24.610 --> 13:27.820
gathered near a Vess and were sealed underground.

13:29.410 --> 13:31.660
So that's the Reaper?

13:32.620 --> 13:33.660
Probably...

13:36.670 --> 13:38.170
Give me a hand!

13:38.170 --> 13:39.590
I-I'm already...

13:39.590 --> 13:42.050
If you don't, I'll tell everyone about your story!

13:42.460 --> 13:44.050
Dammit!

13:45.840 --> 13:47.930
Oh, so it does open up.

13:55.180 --> 13:58.600
All of a sudden it feels like something
more than <i>just</i> the Reaper will show up.

14:05.440 --> 14:08.160
We should go back home.

14:08.660 --> 14:10.370
Hey, ladies.

14:14.330 --> 14:16.790
You also searchin' for the Reaper?

14:17.540 --> 14:20.540
I-I didn't hear any footsteps...

14:21.540 --> 14:24.000
You should be friends with me too.

14:24.000 --> 14:25.300
What's with this—

14:27.800 --> 14:29.220
I'm not a brat.

14:29.220 --> 14:30.890
I'm Isaku Heito.

14:30.890 --> 14:34.100
Friends should call each other by their names.

14:34.850 --> 14:38.310
Come on, say it: Isaku Heito.

14:41.650 --> 14:44.020
Isaku Heito...

14:44.980 --> 14:46.490
Well done!

14:47.110 --> 14:48.490
Thanks.

15:01.080 --> 15:05.210
Jeez, where did Mahmu and Emiru walk off to?

15:07.260 --> 15:08.470
Mahmu?

15:08.470 --> 15:10.720
Emiru isn't with you?

15:10.720 --> 15:13.600
I don't know anything...

15:14.970 --> 15:15.850
Are you all right?

15:16.850 --> 15:19.560
The instructor died...

15:19.560 --> 15:20.810
And next is...

15:20.810 --> 15:21.650
No!

15:21.650 --> 15:22.480
I...

15:24.020 --> 15:25.900
Okay, Mahmu.

15:25.900 --> 15:26.530
Just bite here.

15:42.750 --> 15:45.090
Mahmu, what happened?

15:45.920 --> 15:47.550
I...

15:47.550 --> 15:52.760
Pilot course students from the
investigation team, head to the briefing room.

15:52.760 --> 15:55.550
I'm sure the Reaper is on the move now!

15:56.350 --> 15:57.510
Reaper?

16:00.730 --> 16:03.980
The Reaper is nothing more than a rumor...

16:06.520 --> 16:07.190
What—

16:14.450 --> 16:15.740
What is that?

16:19.790 --> 16:20.700
H-Hold on!

16:21.080 --> 16:22.290
Where are you going?!

16:25.670 --> 16:27.210
This guy, huh?

16:34.840 --> 16:37.010
Wait, stop that!

16:37.010 --> 16:39.470
Isn't it broken somewhere?

16:39.470 --> 16:41.730
It's falling apart, but it's not broken.

16:42.140 --> 16:44.440
You're the one who's broken...

16:50.940 --> 16:52.530
It's still alive after all.

17:39.160 --> 17:40.200
What's happening?

17:49.210 --> 17:52.000
It was Isaku Heito who boarded the Argent.

17:52.000 --> 17:53.920
It seems Hazaki Emiru is all right.

17:54.550 --> 17:55.880
Heito and the Reaper...

17:56.340 --> 17:58.140
What a horrible combination.

17:58.140 --> 17:59.260
What do you mean?

17:59.890 --> 18:04.140
In the past, he killed off everyone in his family.

18:05.520 --> 18:06.640
His own family?

18:08.190 --> 18:10.480
It took in Isaku Heito.

18:10.480 --> 18:13.360
That's just impossible...

18:14.530 --> 18:15.690
Kasane-san?

18:17.490 --> 18:19.200
There's a response from underground at the targets location!

18:38.050 --> 18:40.800
So that's the Reaper...

19:00.360 --> 19:02.530
What in the world... It gives me the creeps.

19:03.410 --> 19:05.490
It's just like a specter.

19:06.790 --> 19:07.330
I'm going in!

19:08.080 --> 19:09.660
Hold on, Raika!

19:10.620 --> 19:12.080
I can't be afraid!

19:12.080 --> 19:14.460
I'm a test pilot for IX.

19:14.460 --> 19:17.050
I'm neither a child nor a criminal!

19:36.780 --> 19:37.570
It's no good!

19:37.570 --> 19:39.190
Anti-Admonition weapons are useless!

19:39.190 --> 19:41.570
Akashi! The Reaper's cockpit!

19:41.570 --> 19:42.700
Cockpit?

19:42.700 --> 19:46.330
There's no way Isaku Heito can control the Reaper like this.

19:46.870 --> 19:48.250
That means...

19:48.700 --> 19:52.210
The Reaper is thrashing about on its own?

20:03.430 --> 20:04.890
Akashi, go before it's too late!

20:05.260 --> 20:07.310
Before it's too late?

20:07.310 --> 20:11.270
I didn't want to let you get close to the Reaper...

20:12.730 --> 20:15.230
Go on, Akashi! Stop the Reaper!

20:18.780 --> 20:19.940
Dammit!

20:25.320 --> 20:26.370
Akashi!

20:34.000 --> 20:36.250
This is Isaku Heito...

20:43.510 --> 20:44.590
Fuck!

20:52.770 --> 20:54.730
You told me to stop this thing, but...

21:10.620 --> 21:12.370
The Lightless Realm?

21:13.620 --> 21:15.040
Akashi...

21:32.930 --> 21:34.560
You're...

21:34.560 --> 21:35.640
You need...

21:38.190 --> 21:40.360
The one that you must defeat...

21:44.650 --> 21:49.160
I've been wanting to head into the
Lightless Realm for some time now.

21:49.160 --> 21:50.280
Right...

21:50.280 --> 21:52.370
Because that's where your big brother...

21:54.370 --> 21:55.460
Akashi!

22:08.930 --> 22:10.050
Did it stop?

22:22.400 --> 22:26.860
The Argent has accepted Akashi...

22:44.800 --> 22:55.430
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.430 --> 22:59.980
In the coldness of the locker room,

22:59.980 --> 23:06.440
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.940 --> 23:12.910
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.910 --> 23:17.450
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.450 --> 23:22.830
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.830 --> 23:27.710
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.710 --> 23:33.430
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.430 --> 23:37.930
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.930 --> 23:43.520
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.520 --> 23:51.610
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Episode 3

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Seam of the Past
